    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the salutation feature: the create-owner request may now include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and owners expose a derived `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, falling back to just `lastName` when no title is supplied.\n\nFollowing the project's existing derived-field convention (like `displayName`/`initials`, which are computed in the mapper from stored fields), I persisted `title` and compute `salutation` on read:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `title` input to `OwnerFields`, and a read-only derived `salutation` to `Owner`. (DTOs are generated from this spec.)\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `title` column (field + getter/setter); MapStruct maps it in/out by name automatically.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `salutation` mapping expression: `title` blank/absent \u2192 `lastName`, else `title + \" \" + lastName`.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 appended a `title` column to the `owners` table.\n- **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 the only seed file using positional inserts; appended a trailing `NULL` to its 10 owner rows to match the new column (h2/postgres use explicit column lists, so they were unaffected).\n\nThe salutation is computed at the mapper (from the stored `title` + `lastName`), so it round-trips correctly through `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}`. The `coreComposesSalutation` test (`title=DR`, `lastName=who` \u2192 `salutation=\"DR who\"`) and the full suite pass.",
